  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal Express has $354M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Federal Express received 962 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $368K. Federal Express obligations are down 39.2% year over year. Federal Express saw its largest buying agency in FY2026 to date as the Department of Veterans Affairs with $199M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $135M. Federal Express sells primarily in the Couriers and Express Delivery Services market, which accounts for $352M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Federal Express also records activity in Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation at $1.5M. Fiscal history shows Federal Express obligations by year: FY21 $305M, FY22 $309M, FY23 $275M, FY24 $677M, FY25 $582M, and FY26 $354M. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year totals.",
